<span id="onepassword-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"
></span><span
  id="onepassword-close-title"
  class="anchor-alias"
  aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid"
  id="onepassword-setup"
  aria-labelledby="onepassword-setup-title"
>
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">a one-time setup</p><h2
      id="onepassword-setup-title"
    >
      Connect the app you already use.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>1. Enable the connection in 1Password.</h3><p>
        Install the 1Password desktop app and sign in. Open Settings →
        Developer. Under <strong>Integrate with the 1Password SDKs</strong>,
        enable <strong>Integrate with other apps</strong>.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>2. Enable login fill in Blanc.</h3><p>
        Open Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → 1Password. Turn on <strong
          >Fill logins from 1Password</strong
        >, enter the email address you use to sign in to 1Password or your
        account ID, and choose <strong>Verify</strong>. Approve Blanc Browser
        when 1Password asks.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>3. Fill when you need it.</h3><p>
        On a website login form, press <kbd>⌥⌘P</kbd> (Option + Command + P), or
        choose View → Fill Login from 1Password. If several Login items match the
        site, choose the one you want. You can also run <code>/1password</code> from
        the Island.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="onepassword-choice-title">
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">you choose when</p><h2
      id="onepassword-choice-title"
    >
      A hint at the form. Fill on request.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>A shortcut beside your browsing.</h3><p>
        Once configured, the Island can show a key hint on a page with a visible
        current-password field. Choose it to start the same login-fill flow.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Your passwords stay in 1Password.</h3><p>
        Blanc never fills automatically or saves the returned credentials. The
        setting and account identifier stay on this device and are excluded from
        Sync. <a href="/privacy">Read how login fill handles data.</a>
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Mac support today.</h3><p>
        The integration is currently available on macOS only. Windows and Linux
        builds do not offer 1Password login fill. It fills matching Login items;
        it does not provide password saving, payment-card filling, or 1Password
        passkeys.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
